SET "bodyEn" = $$<p>Online applications for the Uttar Pradesh Public Service Commission's Review Officer and Assistant Review Officer Examination 2026 opened on 26 October 2026. The commission is recruiting for 501 posts under Advertisement A-4/E-1/2026, and the commission's <a href="https://uppsc.up.nic.in/">official homepage</a> now lists the advertisement as a live advertisement, with the application window running until 26 November 2026.</p>
<p>The commission issued a short notice on 24 October 2026, and the detailed advertisement followed on 26 October 2026. Candidates must complete the commission's One Time Registration before submitting an application, and the commission has set 3 December 2026 as the last date for fee reconciliation and application corrections.</p>
<h2>At a glance</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Conducting body</th><td>Uttar Pradesh Public Service Commission (UPPSC), Prayagraj</td></tr>
<tr><th>Examination</th><td>Samiksha Adhikari / Sahayak Samiksha Adhikari etc. (General / Special Selection) Examination 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Advertisement</th><td>A-4/E-1/2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Posts</th><td>501</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application window</th><td>26 October to 26 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Correction and fee reconciliation last date</th><td>3 December 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Age limit</th><td>21 to 40 years as of 1 July 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application fee</th><td>Rs 125 for General, OBC and EWS; Rs 65 for SC and ST; Rs 25 for PH candidates</td></tr>
<tr><th>Pay</th><td>Level-5 (Rs 29,200 to Rs 64,700) to Level-8 (Rs 47,600 to Rs 1,51,100)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Examination date</th><td>Not announced</td></tr>
<tr><th>Apply at</th><td>uppsc.up.nic.in</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>Why this round matters</h2>
<p>This is the first Review Officer and Assistant Review Officer round since 2023, when 411 posts drew <a href="https://www.thedailyjagran.com/education/news/uppsc-ro-aro-recruitment-2026-notification-out-for-review-officer-assistant-review-officer-500-posts-registration-to-begin-from-oct-26-details-10333902">1,076,004 applicants</a>. The commission said the vacancy count has since risen to 501 after Assistant Review Officer vacancies increased following internal promotions, and the posts are spread across Uttar Pradesh government departments including the Secretariat and the Board of Revenue.</p>
<p>One caution belongs in the same paragraph as the vacancy count. The commission has <a href="https://www.news18.com/education-career/uppsc-ro-aro-recruitment-2026-501-vacancies-announced-applications-begin-today-10397679.html">indicated that the number of vacancies may increase or decrease</a> depending on departmental requirements, so 501 is the announced figure, not a promise that every post will stay open at that number. The advertisement also says that requisitions for similar posts received before the preliminary result is declared may be added to this recruitment.</p>
<h2>Post-wise break-up</h2>
<p>The detailed advertisement gives the full break-up: 495 posts under General Recruitment and 6 under Special Recruitment. The largest shares are Sahayak Samiksha Adhikari in the U.P. Secretariat (261) and Samiksha Adhikari in the U.P. Secretariat (122).</p>
